      "name": "BhaktiBharat Kathmandu daily panchangam",
      "url_pattern": "https://bhaktibharat.org/panchangam/english/{d}-{month}-2026-panchang-english-Kathmandu (month = october for Oct 18-31, november for Nov 1-4)",
      "conventions": "Tithi and nakshatra headline = element running at local noon of the page date (ends AM -> next day, ends PM -> same day). Yoga headline = element running at local midnight of the page date; its Ends field is always same-day. Karana = noon element. Sunrise = local Kathmandu. Oct 18-19 pages use the rich layout, Oct 20 onward the compact layout (identical values). Unlike the Nov window, the tithi and nakshatra 'Starts' fields in this window are genuine and were used for three receipts (noted per-receipt); the yoga 'Starts' field still carries the universal 12:04 AM artifact and is untrusted. Oct 18-19 pages display 'Uttara Phalguni' where canonical is Uttara Ashadha - see flags."
    },
    "hp": {
      "name": "Hamro Patro SSR date pages",
      "url_pattern": "https://www.hamropatro.com/date/2083-7-{bsD} (BS 2083 Kartik = month 7; Kartik 1 = 2026-10-18)",
      "conventions": "Panchang-panel tithi/nakshatra/yoga = udaya (sunrise) element with its end time (may fall next day; samapti weekday disambiguates tithi). Nepali day-words: bihana=AM, diuso/sajh=PM, raat=evening or early-next-morning (00:00-05:59 belongs to the following day). On vriddhi/kshaya-flagged pages (tithi name carries *) the samapti field shows the flagged tithi's START, not its end - see flags section. Karana = udaya element."
    }
  },
